r3-mini: snand u-boot env = NOWHERE (provisioning u-boot ignores the board's env)

The SPI-NAND u-boot is provisioning-only (flash NAND + provision eMMC). With
CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_UBI it read the NAND `ubootenv` volume on every boot — and a
stale *valid* generic env there (distro_bootcmd / loadaddr=0x0) overrode our
compiled defenv, so flash_nand / emmc_install were never loaded and bootcmd ran
the undefined distro_bootcmd.

Switch it to CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE: the provisioning u-boot now ALWAYS uses its
compiled defenv (flash_nand / emmc_install / bootcmd=run emmc_install) and never
touches the board's NAND env. The eMMC *product* u-boot is a separate variant and
keeps CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC for its A/B state — the two are cleanly split.
--- a/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-mini-snand_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7986a_bpi-r3-mini-snand_defconfig
@@ -72,11 +72,8 @@
 CONFIG_CMD_UBI_RENAME=y
 CONFIG_OF_EMBED=y
 CONFIG_ENV_OVERWRITE=y
-CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_UBI=y
-CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT=y
-CONFIG_ENV_UBI_PART="ubi"
-CONFIG_ENV_UBI_VOLUME="ubootenv"
-CONFIG_ENV_UBI_VOLUME_REDUND="ubootenv2"
+CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y
+CONFIG_ENV_SIZE=0x10000
 CONFIG_ENV_RELOC_GD_ENV_ADDR=y
 CONFIG_ENV_USE_DEFAULT_ENV_TEXT_FILE=y
 CONFIG_ENV_DEFAULT_ENV_TEXT_FILE="defenvs/bananapi_bpi-r3-mini_snand_env"
